Well, maybe what you need is a blessed scroll of genocide to get rid
of all those nasty Lichs.   ;^)   But don't waste a wish on that.

I always want to eat every kind of dragon there is (that I don't already
have the corresponding intrinsic for).

I understand that teleport control can be gained by eating (low prob).
If so then I would try to get intrinsic control (I always play a wizard,
so I get it at exp. lvl 18), this will save a ring finger & corresponding
food loss.

Build your stats with blessed potions of gain ability (polymorph potion
piles prolifically).  Build your hit points with a cursed scroll of
genocide (take off your armor & unwield your weapon, then summon a
squad of nurses to "hit" you with new hit-points).

Forgo the gauntlets of power in favor of dexterity (18/** is as good as 25
for strength).  Eat more spinach and royal jelly for your strength.  A cloak
of displacement saves hit-points better than any other single piece of
armor, from my experience.  Jumping boots are great if you get your
speed intrinsically.  Use them to jump over the nasties.

Stormbringer is well-suited to kill the wizard because it drains
levels, and the wizard is level 30.  From hints I've read here, it seems
that you don't necessarilly want to kill the wizard outright (he'll be
back to haunt you again  ;^).  Apparently a potion of paralysis will
stop him without killing him (untried by myself).

Good luck!
